This file records what Calcula bundles and under what terms. It is the place to
check before a release, not a substitute for doing so — the transitive
dependency set below is what the build resolves today, and a version bump can
change it.

================================================================================
The computer algebra engine
================================================================================

Symja / matheclipse (matheclipse-core, matheclipse-parser, and their transitive
dependencies, including JAS)
    https://github.com/axkr/symja_android_library
    License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0).

    Calcula's own code is MIT and does NOT link Symja at compile time. The
    engine is discovered at runtime through a URLClassLoader and ships as plain,
    replaceable jars in a `cas/` directory beside the launcher — so the LGPL's
    relink requirement is satisfied in the simplest available form: drop in a
    different jar and restart. See the reactor root pom.xml for why the split is
    load-bearing rather than cosmetic.

    The full LGPL-3.0 text is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html.

================================================================================
Fonts
================================================================================

Bundled under `com/calcula/fonts/`, unmodified, and used as the interface and
monospaced faces. Both are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which
permits bundling and redistribution within an application.

    Inter          — https://github.com/rsms/inter
                     (c) The Inter Project Authors
    JetBrains Mono — https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
                     (c) JetBrains

    The full OFL 1.1 text is at https://openfontlicense.org.

Typeset formulas do NOT use a bundled font: they are set in JavaFX's logical
"Serif" family, which resolves on every platform without shipping a maths face.

